We also thank the Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Allenhouse Institute of Technology, for providing the facilities and resources necessary to complete this project successfully.

Finally, we thank our family members and friends for their constant support and motivation.

Abstract

Gas leakage is one of the leading causes of fire accidents in homes, industries, laboratories, and commercial kitchens. Detecting combustible gases at an early stage can significantly reduce the risk of explosions and loss of life.

This project presents a Smart Gas Leakage Detection and Alert System using an ESP32 microcontroller, MQ2 gas sensor, and Blynk IoT platform. The MQ2 sensor continuously monitors the surrounding air and detects combustible gases such as LPG, methane, propane, butane, smoke, hydrogen, and alcohol vapors.

The ESP32 processes the sensor readings and compares them with predefined warning and danger thresholds. According to the gas concentration, the system provides visual alerts using Green, Yellow, and Red LEDs, as well as an audible alarm through a buzzer. Sensor readings are transmitted to the Blynk IoT application via Wi-Fi for remote monitoring.

The proposed system is economical, reliable, and easy to implement, making it suitable for domestic and industrial safety applications.

