Chapter 1: Introduction

Gas leakage is a serious issue that can cause explosions, fire accidents, and health hazards. Traditional gas detectors only provide local alarms and cannot notify users remotely.

The rapid growth of the Internet of Things (IoT) enables real-time monitoring of environmental conditions through wireless communication. By integrating sensors, microcontrollers, and cloud platforms, it becomes possible to monitor gas leakage remotely and improve public safety.

This project combines an ESP32 microcontroller with an MQ2 gas sensor to build a low-cost smart gas monitoring system capable of generating local alarms and remote notifications.

Chapter 2: Objectives

The objectives of this project are:

Detect combustible gases in real time.
Provide visual indication using LEDs.
Generate an audible alarm using a buzzer.
Monitor gas concentration remotely using Blynk IoT.
Improve home and industrial safety.
Reduce fire hazards caused by gas leakage.
Chapter 3: Problem Statement

Gas leakage incidents often occur without immediate detection, especially in homes and industries. Existing systems may not provide remote alerts, increasing the risk of accidents.

The objective is to design a low-cost IoT-based solution capable of detecting gas leakage, providing immediate alerts, and allowing remote monitoring.

